{"package":"matplotlib","sourceUrl":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/objects.inv","generatedAt":"2026-09-18T08:23:04.850Z","entries":[{"path":"matplotlib.cm","kind":"package","dispname":"cm","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#module-matplotlib.cm","signature":null,"doc":"Builtin colormaps, colormap handling utilities, and the `ScalarMappable` mixin.\n\n.. seealso::\n\n  :doc:`/gallery/color/colormap_reference` for a list of builtin colormaps.\n\n  :ref:`colormap-manipulation` for examples of how to make\n  colormaps.\n\n  :ref:`colormaps` an in-depth discussion of choosing\n  colormaps.\n\n  :ref:`colormapnorms` for more details about data normalization.","doc_summary":"Builtin colormaps, colormap handling utilities, and the `ScalarMappable` mixin."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ColormapRegistry","kind":"class","dispname":"ColormapRegistry","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ColormapRegistry","signature":"(cmaps)","doc":"Container for colormaps that are known to Matplotlib by name.\n\nThe universal registry instance is `matplotlib.colormaps`. There should be\nno need for users to instantiate `.ColormapRegistry` themselves.\n\nRead access uses a dict-like interface mapping names to `.Colormap`\\s::\n\n    import matplotlib as mpl\n    cmap = mpl.colormaps['viridis']\n\nReturned `.Colormap`\\s are copies, so that their modification does not\nchange the global definition of the colormap.\n\nAdditional colormaps can be added via `.ColormapRegistry.register`::\n\n    mpl.colormaps.register(my_colormap)\n\nTo get a list of all registered colormaps, you can do::\n\n    from matplotlib import colormaps\n    list(colormaps)","doc_summary":"Container for colormaps that are known to Matplotlib by name."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ColormapRegistry.get_cmap","kind":"method","dispname":"get_cmap","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ColormapRegistry.get_cmap","signature":"(self, cmap)","doc":"Return a color map specified through *cmap*.\n\nParameters\n----------\ncmap : str or `~matplotlib.colors.Colormap` or None\n\n    - if a `.Colormap`, return it\n    - if a string, look it up in ``mpl.colormaps``\n    - if None, return the Colormap defined in :rc:`image.cmap`\n\nReturns\n-------\nColormap","doc_summary":"Return a color map specified through *cmap*."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ColormapRegistry.register","kind":"method","dispname":"register","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ColormapRegistry.register","signature":"(self, cmap, *, name=None, force=False)","doc":"Register a new colormap.\n\nThe colormap name can then be used as a string argument to any ``cmap``\nparameter in Matplotlib. It is also available in ``pyplot.get_cmap``.\n\nThe colormap registry stores a copy of the given colormap, so that\nfuture changes to the original colormap instance do not affect the\nregistered colormap. Think of this as the registry taking a snapshot\nof the colormap at registration.\n\nParameters\n----------\ncmap : matplotlib.colors.Colormap\n    The colormap to register.\n\nname : str, optional\n    The name for the colormap. If not given, ``cmap.name`` is used.\n\nforce : bool, default: False\n    If False, a ValueError is raised if trying to overwrite an already\n    registered name. True supports overwriting registered colormaps\n    other than the builtin colormaps.","doc_summary":"Register a new colormap."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ColormapRegistry.unregister","kind":"method","dispname":"unregister","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ColormapRegistry.unregister","signature":"(self, name)","doc":"Remove a colormap from the registry.\n\nYou cannot remove built-in colormaps.\n\nIf the named colormap is not registered, returns with no error, raises\nif you try to de-register a default colormap.\n\n.. warning::\n\n    Colormap names are currently a shared namespace that may be used\n    by multiple packages. Use `unregister` only if you know you\n    have registered that name before. In particular, do not\n    unregister just in case to clean the name before registering a\n    new colormap.\n\nParameters\n----------\nname : str\n    The name of the colormap to be removed.\n\nRaises\n------\nValueError\n    If you try to remove a default built-in colormap.","doc_summary":"Remove a colormap from the registry."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable","kind":"class","dispname":"ScalarMappable","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable","signature":"(norm=None, cmap=None, *, colorizer=None, **kwargs)","doc":"A mixin class to map one or multiple sets of scalar data to RGBA.\n\nThe ScalarMappable applies data normalization before returning RGBA colors from\nthe given `~matplotlib.colors.Colormap`.","doc_summary":"A mixin class to map one or multiple sets of scalar data to RGBA."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.autoscale","kind":"method","dispname":"autoscale","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.autoscale","signature":"(self)","doc":"Autoscale the scalar limits on the norm instance using the\ncurrent array","doc_summary":"Autoscale the scalar limits on the norm instance using the current array"},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.autoscale_None","kind":"method","dispname":"autoscale_None","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.autoscale_None","signature":"(self)","doc":"Autoscale the scalar limits on the norm instance using the\ncurrent array, changing only limits that are None","doc_summary":"Autoscale the scalar limits on the norm instance using the current array, changing only limits that are None"},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.changed","kind":"method","dispname":"changed","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.changed","signature":"(self)","doc":"Call this whenever the mappable is changed to notify all the\ncallbackSM listeners to the 'changed' signal.","doc_summary":"Call this whenever the mappable is changed to notify all the callbackSM listeners to the 'changed' signal."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.colorbar","kind":"property","dispname":"colorbar","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.colorbar","signature":null,"doc":"The last colorbar associated with this object. May be None","doc_summary":"The last colorbar associated with this object. May be None"},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.get_alpha","kind":"method","dispname":"get_alpha","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.get_alpha","signature":"(self)"},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.get_array","kind":"method","dispname":"get_array","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.get_array","signature":"(self)","doc":"Return the array of values, that are mapped to colors.\n\nThe base class `.ScalarMappable` does not make any assumptions on\nthe dimensionality and shape of the array.","doc_summary":"Return the array of values, that are mapped to colors."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.get_clim","kind":"method","dispname":"get_clim","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.get_clim","signature":"(self)","doc":"Return the values (min, max) that are mapped to the colormap limits.","doc_summary":"Return the values (min, max) that are mapped to the colormap limits."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.get_cmap","kind":"method","dispname":"get_cmap","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.get_cmap","signature":"(self)","doc":"Return the `.Colormap` instance.","doc_summary":"Return the `.Colormap` instance."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.norm","kind":"property","dispname":"norm","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.norm","signature":null},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.set_array","kind":"method","dispname":"set_array","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.set_array","signature":"(self, A)","doc":"Set the value array from array-like *A*.\n\nParameters\n----------\nA : array-like or None\n    The values that are mapped to colors.\n\n    The base class `.ScalarMappable` does not make any assumptions on\n    the dimensionality and shape of the value array *A*.","doc_summary":"Set the value array from array-like *A*."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.set_clim","kind":"method","dispname":"set_clim","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.set_clim","signature":"(self, vmin=None, vmax=None)","doc":"Set the norm limits for image scaling.\n\nParameters\n----------\nvmin, vmax : float\n     The limits.\n\n     For scalar data, the limits may also be passed as a\n     tuple (*vmin*, *vmax*) as a single positional argument.\n\n     .. ACCEPTS: (vmin: float, vmax: float)","doc_summary":"Set the norm limits for image scaling."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.set_cmap","kind":"method","dispname":"set_cmap","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.set_cmap","signature":"(self, cmap)","doc":"Set the colormap for luminance data.\n\nParameters\n----------\ncmap : `.Colormap` or str or None","doc_summary":"Set the colormap for luminance data."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.set_norm","kind":"method","dispname":"set_norm","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.set_norm","signature":"(self, norm)","doc":"Set the normalization instance.\n\nParameters\n----------\nnorm : `.Normalize` or str or None\n\nNotes\n-----\nIf there are any colorbars using the mappable for this norm, setting\nthe norm of the mappable will reset the norm, locator, and formatters\non the colorbar to default.","doc_summary":"Set the normalization instance."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.to_rgba","kind":"method","dispname":"to_rgba","docUri":"https://matplotlib.org/stable/api/cm_api.html#matplotlib.cm.ScalarMappable.to_rgba","signature":"(self, x, alpha=None, bytes=False, norm=True)","doc":"Return a normalized RGBA array corresponding to *x*.\n\nIn the normal case, *x* is a 1D or 2D sequence of scalars, and\nthe corresponding `~numpy.ndarray` of RGBA values will be returned,\nbased on the norm and colormap set for this Colorizer.\n\nThere is one special case, for handling images that are already\nRGB or RGBA, such as might have been read from an image file.\nIf *x* is an `~numpy.ndarray` with 3 dimensions,\nand the last dimension is either 3 or 4, then it will be\ntreated as an RGB or RGBA array, and no mapping will be done.\nThe array can be `~numpy.uint8`, or it can be floats with\nvalues in the 0-1 range; otherwise a ValueError will be raised.\nAny NaNs or masked elements will be set to 0 alpha.\nIf the last dimension is 3, the *alpha* kwarg (defaulting to 1)\nwill be used to fill in the transparency.  If the last dimension\nis 4, the *alpha* kwarg is ignored; it does not\nreplace the preexisting alpha.  A ValueError will be raised\nif the third dimension is other than 3 or 4.\n\nIn either case, if *bytes* is *False* (default), the RGBA\narray will be floats in the 0-1 range; if it is *True*,\nthe returned RGBA array will be `~numpy.uint8` in the 0 to 255 range.\n\nIf norm is False, no normalization of the input data is\nperformed, and it is assumed to be in the range (0-1).","doc_summary":"Return a normalized RGBA array corresponding to *x*."},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.Accent","kind":"function","dispname":"Accent","docUri":null,"signature":"(X, alpha=None, bytes=False)"},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.Accent_r","kind":"function","dispname":"Accent_r","docUri":null,"signature":"(X, alpha=None, bytes=False)"},{"path":"matplotlib.cm.Blues","kind":"function","